# the signed C1-LUAD confirmatory-test rule ships as the D3 third-party-timestamp
# record (OSF registration + this GitHub release); its sha256 sidecar ships with it
!review/C1_LUAD_FROZEN_RULE_DRAFT_2026-09-27.md
!review/C1_LUAD_FROZEN_RULE_DRAFT_2026-09-27.md.sha256
# its registration receipt, the post-signature addenda the rule (section 7.4) names, and
# the logs its D3 paper wording says are in the repository (desensitised copies)
!review/C1_LUAD_D3_RECEIPT_2026-10-01.md
!review/C1_LUAD_ADDENDA.md
!review/C1_LUAD_ADDENDA.md.sha256
!review/c1_luad_logs/
!review/c1_luad_logs/**
# the dated pre-specification of the post hoc batch-axis analyses, published (with the
# scripts and label files its section F freezes) before any of those jobs is submitted
!review/POSTHOC_BATCH_AXES_PRESPEC_2026-10-02.md
!review/POSTHOC_BATCH_AXES_PRESPEC_2026-10-02.md.sha256
!review/BATCH_AXES_SCOPING_2026-10-02/
review/BATCH_AXES_SCOPING_2026-10-02/*
!review/BATCH_AXES_SCOPING_2026-10-02/pathdb/
review/BATCH_AXES_SCOPING_2026-10-02/pathdb/*
!review/BATCH_AXES_SCOPING_2026-10-02/pathdb/download_log.tsv

